      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "KING BART (3) finished fifth last start, beaten 13 metres at this track over 2180m. Talented and has plenty of upside. Likely to get all the favours from this nice draw. Good enough to take out a race like this. GEMMY LOU (1) was responsible for a very good effort last time over 2180m at this track, finishing third and just 1.3 metres from the winner. No excuses from this advantageous draw. Won't find this any harder and she can grab a win. OUR SWEET TRIXIE NZ (8) is on the radar after her last-start fourth over 2200m at Launceston five days ago. STANTON BREAK (7) did a good job to finish third first-up two runs ago then broke in the run and finished tailed off at the latest appearance over 2180m at this track. Gets a soft run on the inside of the second line but may need luck at some point. Meets a similar line up so if he behaves a big run is likely.",
